NO RECORDED FIXTURE — NOT A SUPPORTED FORMAT (BR-INT-033).
The codec `bai2` is registered BY NAME ONLY so a manifest may cite it and a picker may offer it. Its first real file is recorded from the bank, as a BAI2 statement on connect day, by wave I (the same bank file twice), and its encoder or decoder lands in the same commit. Nothing in this folder is a sample somebody typed: a typed sample would make the conformance kit say *supported* about a format nothing reads.
